{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","soma"],"title":"Sumanā","html":"<article id='thig1.14'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Therīgāthā 1.14 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Nuns 1.14 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Verses of the Elder Bhikkhunīs </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Chapter of the Ones </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sumanātherīgāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sumanā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Verses of the Elder Sumanā </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Dhātuyo dukkhato disvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Having seen the elements as suffering, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>“Having seen the elements as suffering, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mā jātiṁ punarāgami; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>don’t get reborn again. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>do not return to birth. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Bhave chandaṁ virājetvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>When you’ve discarded desire for rebirth, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Having destroyed the fervor for existence, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>upasantā carissasī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you will live at peace. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>you will walk in peace.” </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Sumanā therī …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>The Elder Sumanā </span></p></article>"}
